set.body:
Objective: extend the completed typed operator-compression core with an honest variational and fold-safe fitting language.

Mathematical form:
- certified operator policies realize statistical operators before program construction;
- a Parameterization maps free variables to semantic parameters;
- typed target expressions inspect one or more semantic parameters;
- Functionals express soft preferences;
- FeasibleSets express hard conditions;
- solver lowering preserves the requested public semantics and records every equivalence.

The abstractions remain distinct:
1. pure typed maps and target expressions;
2. parameterizations;
3. operator policies;
4. scalar or extended-real functionals;
5. feasible sets;
6. ModelSpec lifecycle for fitted preprocessing, estimation, tuning, alignment, and transformation.

This epic begins only after the finite operator-core release gate. It is decomposed into closeable families:
- target/functionals/sets foundation and program symmetry inference;
- linear-quadratic pullbacks;
- explicit charts, sparsity, groups, and separable proximal cases;
- exact parameterizations and gauges;
- general composed nonsmooth terms with split/primal-dual lowering;
- certified operator policies including joint covariance shrinkage;
- fold-safe ModelSpec lifecycle.

Constitutional rules:
- no coordinate property without a chart and no quadratic norm without geometry;
- operator shrinkage is not parameter ridge;
- parameterization is not regularization;
- penalize and constrain remain distinct publicly;
- projection and proximal operations are solver capabilities, not semantic maps;
- a simple prox for a functional never licenses a false prox for its composition;
- invariance is inferred from the complete term and complete program;
- every family ships with a lowering, an independent oracle or external parity fixture, JVM/JS tests, provenance, and an honest solver guarantee.

Completion: all finite children close at a committed tip; requested and lowered programs are inspectable; cross-validation refits every learned operation inside training folds; solver claims distinguish global, convex, stationary, local, heuristic, and unresolved results.
